00:05:55.920 --> 00:06:00.960
and cross your fingers that it won't hallucinate an exception. No way, you must enforce that rule

77
00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:06.880
deterministically in your actual application code. And this is exactly where gates come into play.

78
00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:12.240
A gate is a programmatic quality check sitting right between the steps of your prompt chain.

79
00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:17.600
Imagine an AI agent drafting an outline and another step writing a document based on that

80
00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:23.680
outline. A gate inspects the outline first. If it's garbage, the gate stops or revises the workflow

81
00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:29.360
early. Skipping gates means that bad data just flows silently downstream, compounding your errors

82
00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:35.360
until the entire output is completely useless. Section five, reliability in production.

