00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:41.360
pass. Why do we do it this way? Because two focused, smaller passes will catch the critical bugs that

94
00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:47.680
one giant context-stuffed review pass simply buries. And out in production, every single piece

95
00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:52.080
